WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.200
For a show to be good, is it always necessary to&nbsp;
have a complex plot and a deep cast of characters?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:13.920
Can masterful visual and sound-production&nbsp;
elevate an average story to a great one?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.440
I believe Kimetsu no Yaiba proves it can.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.560
I feel like there are only two types&nbsp;
of opinions about Kimetsu no Yaiba:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:40.960
Either you love it as one of the best anime of the&nbsp;
decade or you hate it as an over-hyped story with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.800
little to back it up. So now after the movie, that&nbsp;
broke absolutely broke the box-offices in Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.080
and with the widely-anticipated&nbsp;
release of the second season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.120
I finally want to share my honest thoughts on&nbsp;
this highly controversial Anime - spoiler free.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.760
Hi my name is Manu, I'm getting really tired&nbsp;
of all the Demon Slayer Merch here in Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.760
seriously, every convenient store&nbsp;
has some chocolate or beverage with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.080
something from this series, but nonetheless,&nbsp;
I want to convince you today that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.000
absolutely worth watching Kimitsu no Yaiba,&nbsp;
with a heavy emphasis on the watching part.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.920
Before we can get into the part of this&nbsp;
show that I absolutely love and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.360
ultimately made me recommend this show,&nbsp;
I want to address some criticism I have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.280
This anime set new standards in some aspects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:34.080
but is quite underwhelming in others, which I&nbsp;
feel leads to the polarised opinions around it.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:40.560
The biggest criticism you hear around the story is&nbsp;
its writing. But that's such a general criticism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.360
that it physically pains me, whenever someone says&nbsp;
it. Writing consists of many parts. The world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.880
the premise, the plot, the characters, the&nbsp;
dialog and much much more. That being said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.480
I promised I would start with the negative.&nbsp;
One of my favourite things in storytelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.680
are great characters. People that are&nbsp;
relatable, detestable or inspiring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.560
but generally feel like real people who go&nbsp;
on some sort of journey throughout the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.560
And I honestly gotta say that demon slayer does&nbsp;
not have great character writing. Tanjiro is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:22.640
interesting take on the Shonen Hero Trope, one of&nbsp;
the better characters in the story and definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:29.040
not as terrible as some claim. But he also&nbsp;
doesn't impact me as much on a personal level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:36.640
as a Luffy or Itadori would and in a way is almost&nbsp;
a little bit 'too good', where there are very few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:49.840
morally questionable actions from his side,&nbsp;
that make him feel more like a real person.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.320
Almost all of the characters have a distinctive&nbsp;
quirk that makes them unique, but at the same time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:03.280
lack proper characterisation. Zenitsu is probably&nbsp;
the most annoying aspect of the show for me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.720
because even with his backstory we don't&nbsp;
really get a good explanation as for why he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.560
behaves this way, and honestly the joke with his&nbsp;
character as an over-the-top coward drags on way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.040
to long. And there is literally no&nbsp;
redeeming aspect to his character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.640
Similarly Inosuke's quirk is also a bit too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.800
however compared to Zenitsu he has a lot&nbsp;
more character development in that regard.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.960
Another thing that bothered me was that many&nbsp;
of the antagonists get flash backs to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:47.040
them relatable, however with very poor timing,&nbsp;
only after they already have been defeated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.120
which sort of misses the point of&nbsp;
making us sympathise with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.840
Nezuko, who is the star of the show&nbsp;
in a way, is extremely lovable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:07.920
yes, but doesn't have a single line of dialogue&nbsp;
throughout the series, even though demons can talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:14.240
and we have other examples of good demons, not&nbsp;
eating humans. So why does Nezuko wear a muzzle?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.720
In general there a number of inconsistencies like&nbsp;
these throughout the story. And at some points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.000
I find the pacing of the plot very poorly&nbsp;
chosen, where some fights drag on too long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.440
while important character moments are cut&nbsp;
short or overshadowed by badly-timed comedy.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:44.240
Demon slayer is not perfect and I think&nbsp;
criticising certain aspects of the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.880
is absolutely justified, and&nbsp;
it's a shame because the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:55.040
could be so much more with better character&nbsp;
writing. However, now with all that being said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:00.240
why do I still love and strongly&nbsp;
recommend that you watch this anime?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.560
Well first of all, next to character&nbsp;
and pace, there is a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:10.080
really decent writing in this as well.&nbsp;
The premise of the story is pretty good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.200
as we follow Tanjiro's quest to find a cure&nbsp;
for his sister, where we follow him growing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:21.120
up and learning about the world around him. It's&nbsp;
a classic Shounen arc, but very well executed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:41.200
There is a great balance of characters, with&nbsp;
a very refreshing take on female character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.240
not following the big-boobed&nbsp;
damsel in distress pattern,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.200
but actually introducing a very&nbsp;
unique and impressive cast of male&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:55.200
and female characters alike. And the anime&nbsp;
doesn't shy away form graphic imagery and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.840
a darker sub-tone. Two things that also made&nbsp;
Jujutsu Kaisen stand out. Tanjiro's motivation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.240
is clear from the start&nbsp;
and we can fully understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.160
why he does what he does. This allows us to&nbsp;
explore the world of this anime with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:29.120
which is the first thing about Kimetsu no&nbsp;
Yaiba where it outshines many other stories.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:36.880
The setting and story world of this anime&nbsp;
is absolutely fantastic. I am a huge fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:42.880
of world building and chasing Edo-period Japan&nbsp;
was the perfect choice for this in my opinion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:49.120
This way we get the best of both worlds,&nbsp;
rural med-eval Japan as well as bright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.280
vivid cities. Times are changing&nbsp;
and we see tradition and katana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:59.200
meeting electricity and progress. We see&nbsp;
the demons integrating into this new world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:15.840
way better than the demon slayer organisation and&nbsp;
the challenges that come with a changing country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.480
But for me most importantly, we get the&nbsp;
beautiful aesthetic of Edo period Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:30.640
that offers most of the romanticised&nbsp;
image of Japan, many of us love.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:36.480
The landscapes are beautiful, the towns and&nbsp;
cities are beautiful, and despite the constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:41.440
threat of the demons, there is a certain&nbsp;
sense of piece and stability to this world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.480
Do you know that warm feeling you associate&nbsp;
with wonderfully drawn anime landscapes? Well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:53.680
demon slayer is that for every single episode.&nbsp;
It's a fantastic, if admittedly romanticised,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:59.840
glimpse into a version of Japan that you don't&nbsp;
see all too often in Anime, that Japanese people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:05.520
are very proud of, which partly explains&nbsp;
the crazy success it had domestically.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:12.960
However, this already gets to the core of this&nbsp;
video. For me, this world only truly comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:19.200
live like this in the Anime. The main reason&nbsp;
this story become such a hit and was able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:25.200
distinguish itself form its competition, was&nbsp;
in large parts thanks to studio Ufotable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:34.080
who brought this world to life. I really&nbsp;
can’t praise the studio enough because that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:39.680
how big their contribution has been. You&nbsp;
can pause the anime at almost any point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:45.280
and it looks like a wallpaper. The&nbsp;
world feels vibrant and alive. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.960
character designs are colourful and unique and&nbsp;
combined with fantastic voice acting as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:09:07.840
as detail-rich facial expressions make up for a&nbsp;
lot of the characterisation missing in the manga.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.880
The production team managed to find a&nbsp;
near flawless balance between 2D and 3D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:20.880
seamlessly blending the two to allow for new and&nbsp;
exciting camera moments and action sequences as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:29.280
well as stunning ambient lighting, perfecting what&nbsp;
many other anime struggle with. Visually, Demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:37.360
Slayer easily outperforms most competition of the&nbsp;
last few years. It's truly a visual masterpiece.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.640
The score, created by Yuki Kajiura&nbsp;
and Go Shiina, is pretty much perfect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:49.840
with a rich variety of tracks that by themselves&nbsp;
lift the plot and storyline to a higher level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:04.400
The openings by the artist Lisa&nbsp;
are so popular here in Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:09.680
that you basically hear them every day&nbsp;
SOMEWHERE playing on some radio station.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:15.920
All of it accentuated by great sound design,&nbsp;
that complements the score perfectly.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.640
Interestingly enough, Demon Slayer not only won&nbsp;
Anime of the year at the Chrunchyroll Awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:29.680
but also 'Best Fight Scene'. And I think&nbsp;
that this is the real reason this Anime is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:35.280
as successful as it is. The outstanding&nbsp;
work of the visual and sound-department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:41.840
came to full fruition with the many action and&nbsp;
fighting scenes this anime has. Every-time Tanjiro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:47.920
swings unleashes his water-breathing, it is&nbsp;
followed by a visual firework of these beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:53.840
lush blue ink-like waves juxtaposed&nbsp;
against a photorealistic background.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:59.520
That is just breath-taking every&nbsp;
time I see it. Even slow-motion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:13.840
which is often used a bit awkwardly in Japanese&nbsp;
media, is perfect. Just look at this scene.&nbsp;[]

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.640
This is some real eye-candy. So in the&nbsp;
end, while the writing in the Manga is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:26.160
far from impeccable and in some parts is a little&nbsp;
disappointing, the concept of the story overall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:31.040
is solid. And taken to the screen with&nbsp;
breathtaking work from the production team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.240
Kimetsu no Yaiba in my opinion is a must-see,&nbsp;
though you can skip the scenes with Zenitsu in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:41.920
my opinion. It is easily bingable, and now that&nbsp;
season two is out with the pleasure district arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:47.920
I can't wait to dive back into this&nbsp;
Edo-period wonder-world and hunt some demons.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:51.280
If you made it until here, that's the&nbsp;
universe telling you to subscribe.

